{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:eb105f601c133973","name":"Leeches","source":{"id":"source:reference-eb105f601c133973","title":"Leeches","revision":26543,"timestamp":"2025-03-26T06:29:13Z","sha256":"37f8ca4ddb0dee1cd95f687839f55a546d54bcedb6ddba9e1dc3474070e47522","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26543","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Leeches&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-eb105f601c133973","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Tiny parasites attach to your skin and suck your fluids for nourishment."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["At some point, creatures traveling through a swamp must trudge through water. When they do, they might encounter Leeches. Leeches have a way of slipping past the best defenses and latching onto the skin under a creature's armor or clothing. Not only do these parasites cause damage to the creatures they attack, they can cause a group to be hesitant to enter other bodies of water, giving opponents a chance to strike.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Leeches Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A being begins its turn within an area containing Leeches.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +4 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," - (-1 step on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},")\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," Each round at the start of the target's turn, until the Leeches are removed.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Treat Injury"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Treat_Injury","referenceId":"reference:f1b9875c2302ce61"}," (DC 19):"]}," The character safely removes the Leeches."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," Leeches ignore the effects of a creature's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"},", unless the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"}," is natural or airtight.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
